{
 "encounter_id": "00852",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Doctor, thank you. It's Rory, he's fifteen, he did his knee playing rugby six weeks ago, and he's still limping."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Hello Rory. Which knee, and what happened?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "The left. I got tackled from the side, and my knee twisted, and I felt a pop."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Was there swelling, immediately?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yeah. Within an hour. It was huge."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "It was like a balloon. We took him to the emergency department, they said sprain, gave him a brace."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How is it now?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's better, but it gives way on stairs, and it clicks, and I can't straighten it fully."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is there any locking, where it gets stuck?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Once or twice. It catches."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any numbness, or any pain at night?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. Nothing like that."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any fever, or redness on the knee?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What have you been taking for the pain?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Ibuprofen, 200 mg, three times a day, with food."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, it's 400 mg, Rory. I gave him two tablets. And paracetamol, 500 mg, when he needs it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll note that you and Mum gave different doses of ibuprofen, and I'll check which. Any other conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He has mild asthma, hay fever, and eczema."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check pulse and the rest. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 72, blood pressure 118 over 70, temperature 36.6, weight 62 kilos.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Fine? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fine. Rory, lie down on the couch, and I'll examine the knee. Tell me when it hurts. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay.",
   "pause": 20.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's a little fluid in the left knee, and tenderness over the inner side of the joint line, and when I twist it, I get a click and pain. The ligaments feel stable."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "What does that mean? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It suggests a tear in the cartilage, the meniscus, rather than a ligament. Considering the twist and the locking, I'd say this is a probable meniscal tear."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Will he need surgery? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Possibly. I'd like to arrange an MRI scan of the left knee, to see exactly what's torn."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Can I play? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No rugby for now. Keep the knee moving, gentle exercises, and no twisting or running."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "He won't like that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I know, Rory, and I'm sorry. But playing on a torn meniscus can make it worse. I'll refer you to the physio as well."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the MRI result."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Three weeks. Thanks, doctor. ~"
  }
 ],
